# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=rogue:assassination style=auto size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried (behaves as fresh -- #273
# is still open: carried never actually survives a separate playbot
# invocation because the dev-server port is keyed off the process pid).
#
# This exact spec/style/size/difficulty/save combination was already run once
# (2026-09-27T23:50:00Z, playtest/plans/2026-09-28-17.play) at view
# 844x390,touch -- a short landscape phone. The only axis this session can add
# anything on is the viewport: 820x1180,touch is a tall portrait tablet, far
# wider than any viewport #386 (AUTO's hit-circle overlapping ability:4/5,
# filed 2026-10-28) was measured on. #386's own numbers are clamp-floor
# dependent at 390px width (btnR hits its 21px floor); at 820px width
# btnR = clamp(820*0.031, 21, 26) = 25.42 is NOT floor-clamped, so this is a
# genuinely different point on the formula, not a re-run of the same inputs.
# Worth a `ui` read on the fight screen before running the evening, to see
# whether the overlap #386 names is a floor-clamp artifact (and so narrow-
# phone-only) or survives at a size where the clamp never engages.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
ui
shot ui-check

evening auto 200 8
state
shot end
says
bill
